Implemented:
news_fetch.php
- The HTTP 403 diagnostic is now emitted only when the article body is still
  empty after the feed and reader-mirror fallbacks. Previously it was printed
  as soon as Medium challenged the direct page request, even though the
  freedium mirror recovered the complete story, so /news and /medium showed
  false failures.
- Added articleBodyIsPlaceholder(): a reader mirror answers HTTP 200 for a
  deleted or moved story with a short "We couldn't find the article..." page.
  Such a page is no longer cached or treated as an article body, and a
  placeholder cached by an older run is refetched instead of served.
- Added isNonArticleUrl(): Google News' site:medium.com feed occasionally
  indexes an author profile (for example https://medium.com/@japan.gently.told).
  Profile/landing links are recognized as non-articles, are not fetched, do not
  produce a 403 error, and are dropped from the story list.
- Empty bodies for reader-mirror publishers still use the short failure TTL, and
  detail requests still retry them, so a transient mirror failure recovers on
  the next open.

Verified:
- `news_fetch.php --json --source medium --limit 6` now prints no stderr
  diagnostics; the profile entry is dropped and the remaining five stories
  stream full bodies (12-74 paragraphs each).
- The reported NVIDIA story loads 12 paragraphs / 1 image on demand with no
  error.
- The requested https://medium.com/@chrisdunlop_37984/so-shall-we-give-up-then-2d095fa8c410
  loads 31 paragraphs / 1 image through the reader mirror with no error.
- php -l passes.
